WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
*sigh* This movie… doesn’t make sense.

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:04.720
This movie doesn’t make sen--

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.370
Welcome back to Things You Missed.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.810
Last time we covered Pet Sematary -- this
time I’m taking on the movie-only sequel

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.110
Pet Sematary II.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.439
The way the logo is animated calls back to
the blue light that shines from the Mic Mac

00:00:18.439 --> 00:00:23.029
burial grounds in the first one, but the actual
tone of the movie does not remind of the first

00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:24.029
one.

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:27.329
It opens on a Hollywood movie set where this
woman is reaching to open a coffin it seems

00:00:27.329 --> 00:00:30.720
-- a little bit of a hint that maybe her coffin
is going to be pried open later on.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.539
But before she can open it, this hand reaches
for her (as part of the horror movie they’re

00:00:34.539 --> 00:00:36.719
filming), and later on we get a better look
at that prop.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.320
It looks exactly like the hand that appeared
a couple years beforehand in IT.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:50.280
I later found out that it actually is the
same exact prop, so props to them for reusing

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.980
that, pun intended.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.170
Another possible Stephen King reference can
be seen on the slate, which displays the title

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.530
of this movie within the movie: Castle of
Terror.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:01.070
It could be a reference to Castle Rock, which
is a location in Maine that shows up in a

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:03.989
bunch of Stephen King novels and later got
its own TV show.

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:05.250
Thirty-three takes?

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.250
Yikes.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.650
Maybe Renee was lucky to have gotten the early
ticket off that set.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:12.520
What I want to know is who saw this woman
getting electrocuted and decided, ‘you know

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:13.520
what?

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.290
I’m gonna knock over this 1K just to add
to the noise.'

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:19.390
We then meet Renee’s husband, who is a veterinarian,
which I found interesting because Louis, from

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:22.300
the first movie, specifically says that he’s
not a vet at one point.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:29.060
“I'm trying to tell myself that I buried
him alive.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:31.119
I’m not a vet.”

00:01:31.119 --> 00:01:35.399
This kid has to make the decision to put down
his beloved dog -- and Dr. Mathews is faced

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:37.660
with a similar decision at the end of the
movie.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.969
So then like 2 hours after the funeral of
his wife, Dr. Mathews is already checking

00:01:40.969 --> 00:01:42.350
out his attractive young housekeeper.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:45.869
If he had been able to keep his eyes off of
her, he would have noticed the name of the

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:47.180
moving company -- Mayflower.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:50.820
Historically, the Mayflower was the name of
one of the ships that brought the first European

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.200
settlers to America.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.719
These settlers ended up driving away the Native
American groups that already lived there -- and

00:01:55.719 --> 00:02:00.270
this movie is basically about white settlers
defiling an ancient Indian burial ground.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.051
But I’m with Dr. Mathews on this one, the
hot chick is much more interesting to look

00:02:03.051 --> 00:02:04.051
it.

00:02:04.051 --> 00:02:06.250
She almost gets killed by a box of Renee’s
stuff...

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.439
“Look out!

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:08.640
Look out!”

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.710
Which sets up her eventually later getting
killed by Renee herself.

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:16.410
Dr. Mathews’ son Jeff tags along as he goes
to work, where he basically sums up the entire

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:17.410
movie.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.560
“This isn’t too bad.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.780
It’s uh, pretty bad.”

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.819
For example here’s a newspaper from Coweta,
Georgia, where they filmed the movie even

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:30.290
though it’s supposed to take place in Maine.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:34.260
The town sheriff brings his step-son to get
his dog Zowie checked out by the new doc,

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.340
even though he end up shooting the dog THE
VERY NEXT NIGHT.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:42.340
“Come on Amanda, stop looking at me like
that, he’s had ample warning about that

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:42.840
dog!”

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.920
So what was the point of bringing him to the
vet if you wanted him dead?

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.870
I just don’t understand the logic there.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:51.720
Also Jeff tries to bring his cat to school
and it gets taken by the bullies.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.010
I only bring it up because I’ll probably
never get to use the work “catnap” again,

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:58.250
and because you might have missed this display
dedicated to Jeff’s mother.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:01.690
I guess it makes sense that she’d be kind
of a hero in such a small town if she made

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.549
it as a B-list actress in Hollywood.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:06.720
Also, when the bullies are running away you
can get a little glimpse of the mascot of

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:07.720
the Jr High school.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.599
It’s the Lumberjacks, which may be another
reference to Native Americans vs European

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:13.770
settlers theme that I mentioned earlier.

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:17.380
During the bike chase that ensues, they ride
by the Creed house, even though it looks nothing

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.159
like the house from the first movie.

00:03:19.159 --> 00:03:23.450
Then Jeff goes to look for the cat in a Pet
Sematary that looks nothing like the Pet Sematary.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.709
Also, the deadfall looks nothing like the
deadfall from the first one.

00:03:26.709 --> 00:03:31.099
It also doesn’t make sense how the main
bully, Clyde Parker, which is an excellent

00:03:31.099 --> 00:03:34.379
bully name by the way, had time to hide the
cat all the way in the Pet Sematary, I mean

00:03:34.379 --> 00:03:37.850
Jeff and the sheriff’s son, Drew, were on
his tail the entire time, like I don’t when

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:38.850
that happened.

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:42.680
But anyway, Jeff finds his cat, and he and
Drew bond over a mutual dislike for their

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:46.439
step-parents / sexy housekeeper basically
step-mom kind of thing.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.240
“The first day of school is always the hardest.”

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:51.700
“You’re not my mother.”

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:56.060
*sad music*

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.730
Jeff and Drew go to bury Zowie.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:01.501
At this point you shouldn’t be surprised
that it looks nothing like the burial ground

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:02.501
from the first one.

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:05.020
In the following scene we see the inside of
Drew’s room.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.920
I’m guessing he’s supposed to be from
Seattle or something, because he’s got a

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:11.621
poster for SeaFair, which takes place in Seattle
and there’s a Mariners pennant near his

00:04:11.621 --> 00:04:12.621
door.

00:04:12.621 --> 00:04:15.650
This could also be part of the reason he and
Jeff become friends, both being transplants

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.540
from the West Coast, though it’s not explained
at all during the movie.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:22.520
His parents are at the door to let him know
that Zowie is back, and his mom gives Dr.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.040
Mathews a call to take a look at him.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.900
While Zowie is staying at the Matthews’
house, he turns up in the middle of the night

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.940
in Jeff’s room looking all SCP-1471.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:40.850
The next part takes place on Halloween, which
was good to see because the first Pet Sematary

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:44.830
movie skips over Halloween, but in the book
it’s actually an important scene where Jud

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:48.470
Crandall’s wife Norma has a heart attack
and Louis saves her life, an event that Jud

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:52.020
would later cite as part of the reason he
felt he had to help Louis revive his daughter’s

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.640
cat by introducing him to the Mic Mac burial
ground.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:59.110
Clyde Parker gives everyone an IMDB summary
of the first movie in ghost-story form as

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:03.260
they sit around a fire at the Pet Sematary,
when the sheriff comes and breaks up the party

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:07.200
so he can punish his son with a little bit
of domestic violence, but Zowie comes to the

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.800
rescue and tears his freaking throat out.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:12.000
This is where things just go off the rails.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.660
Jeff and Drew have a sudden change of heart
and decide to bring the sheriff back using

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:16.840
the Mic Mac grounds.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:19.570
He comes back as a much nicer guy for some
reason..?

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:23.940
I guess that’s what happens when the person
who dies is already more evil than The Wendigo.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.700
Back in Dr. Mathews’s office, he get back
the results of Zowie’s blood test, which

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:31.770
say that the blood came from a dead animal
as the ironic “Natural Life Pet Products”

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:33.230
sign hangs over his head.

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:36.230
Yeah… there’s nothing natural about this
doggo’s life anymore.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.590
Wait, wait, hold on right there.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:38.580
Play that back.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:41.620
Does he just start casually eating dog treats?

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:42.630
What is wrong with this guy?

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:47.070
I mean, I’ve accidentally eaten a dog treat
before and let me just say they’re not good.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.960
Dr. Mathews discovers that Zowie has escaped
and stops by the school to go let Jeff and

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:51.960
Drew know.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:55.490
Does anyone else thing these two deserve their
own 2000s Nickelodeon sitcom?

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:57.450
"Well I never thought..."

00:05:57.450 --> 00:06:01.880
Dr. Mathews go to visit the former Ludlow
veterinarian, who has taken up taxidermy.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.360
Sounds like the villain of a whole nother
horror movie.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.450
But he goes to ask about the dead animal blood.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:10.180
The old vet tells him this happened once before
with the Creed’s cat Church from the first

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:11.180
movie.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:14.721
Church does go to the vet to get fixed, but
that’s before he died, and there’s no

00:06:14.721 --> 00:06:17.220
indication of Louis taking him to the vet
after that.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:20.960
The old vet does have a pair of antlers mounted
on his door, which could be this movie’s

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:25.270
tiny Wendigo reference, just like the mantle-piece
in Jud’s room was in the first one.

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:29.300
Meanwhile the sheriff isn’t trying to kill
anyone but he’s completely lost it.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:35.340
Yeah.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:39.960
While Jeff is over at Drew’s house for dinner,
Dr. Mathews sulks in grievance; watching movies

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:40.960
that his wife was in.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:45.051
This is actually a real movie that the actress
who played Renee was in called Once Upon A

00:06:45.051 --> 00:06:46.051
Time In America.

00:06:46.051 --> 00:06:49.000
I’m kind of impressed they didn’t just
take the whole Bride of Chucky route and just

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.930
have Danlanne Fluegelle in the movie as herself.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.590
The next day after Josh and... ohhhh...

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:54.889
I just did that...

00:06:54.889 --> 00:06:58.960
The next day after Jeff and Drew get done
hanging out and being angsty, Drew notices

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:03.120
excellently named bully Clyde Parker coming
after his friend and performs one of the most

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:06.500
impressive athletic feats in cinema history.

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:20.160
Haha, the best part is that’s actually the
music.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:23.660
Clyde has some weird fascination with bike
spoke related injuries…

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:25.820
"There was a little accident.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:29.320
She was trying to get away.

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:31.180
Her head got caught in the spokes."

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:35.160
... and just before Jeff’s face gets chopped
up, he’s inexplicably saved by a zombie

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:36.160
sheriff.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.930
Who then completely does a 180 and starts
killing everyone he sees.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.940
I never claimed that this movie made sense.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:43.870
He temporarily turns into Jack Torrance from
The Shining.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:46.020
“I’m gonna bash your head in.”

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.120
“I’m just gonna bash your brains in.”

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.640
"****ing stupid!:

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:56.080
"Here's Johnny!"

00:07:58.900 --> 00:07:59.820
"Mom!"

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.400
Hey, you know what’s strange?

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:11.660
In Pet Sematary, the road is constantly filled
with passing trucks.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:13.700
In fact that’s kind of like a main point
of that movie.

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:18.840
But we’ve seen plenty of road shots, and
there hasn’t been one single tru-- oh wait.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:19.960
I see what’s gonna happen.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:38.240
*sad music*

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:42.720
So the sheriff decides to revive Clyde and
Renee for some reason -- I mean, he does explain

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:46.990
why he wants Renee, but at this point it really
just seems like he's doing random stuff.

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:50.070
The only thing I found that seem to kind of
explain his behaviour, is because the Wendigo

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:54.360
never actually appeared in the first movie,
it seems like the director Mary Lambert could

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:57.400
be going for a demonic possession type of
thing instead.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:01.140
This cross that is usually upright in the
sheriff’s house is now inverted, and it

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:05.060
looks like he went a little crazy with the
chainsaw offscreen...

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:06.700
And the lawnmower?

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:10.520
I’m not sure if this is supposed to be a
reference or not, but the way Jeff is sitting

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:14.040
in this chair reminds me a lot of Claire from
Black Christmas.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:17.610
This movie ends the same way as the first
one essentially, with all the zombies showing

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:19.350
up, and then dying in a fire.

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:21.700
Except this time the fire is started by the
zombies.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.550
The sheriff goes through all this trouble
to bring these people back, and then they

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:26.270
basically just want to die again?

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:30.140
There’s a clear chance for Renee to escape
right here, but she just wants them to stay

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:31.280
with her as she burns in the fire.

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:34.490
So I’ll wrap up this video how I started
it by saying…

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:36.270
“This movie makes no sense!”

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:40.690
But we’re not done with Pet Sematary yet,
because the remake is coming out in just a

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:44.430
couple weeks so check out the video on the
left to hear about the complete history of

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:48.760
the Pet Sematary Wendigo and make sure you’re
subscribed to CZsWorld to hear about all the

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:53.270
things you might have missed in the 2019 Pet
Sematary, ring the deatbell for notifications

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:55.490
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.680
Assuming we both survive.

